# Hearthlight — git tracks the INSTRUCTION LAYER (the reusable system) only.
# Project work + media + secrets stay out (rights-constrained, large, or sensitive).

# ─── Secrets — never commit ──────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.env
**/.env
*apikey*
*api_key*
*secret*
*.key

# ─── Project work — NOT in the system repo ───────────────────────
# Per-project creative work + media + the storyteller's material live only in WSL,
# not in version control. The repo is the reusable pipeline, not the films.
projects/

# ─── Sync internals & logs ───────────────────────────────────────
_sync/logs/
*.log
SYNC-CHANGELOG.md

# ─── Scratch & transient work ────────────────────────────────────
# Ad-hoc inspection scratch and empty temp dirs left by test runs.
.artifact-work/
test-tmp/
.test-tmp/
# The dashboard and image-prompt suites build their TemporaryDirectory INSIDE the
# tests folder rather than the system temp dir, and cleanup fails on a mounted
# Windows folder -- so a failed run leaves tmpXXXXXXXX/ behind, unremovable from
# the sandbox. Ignored so `git add -A` cannot swallow them. Added 2026-08-10.
**/tests/tmp*/
node_modules/
.venv-stt/

# ─── Checkpoint internals ────────────────────────────────────────
# The dated checkpoint .md files ARE tracked (they are the history).
# The raw fact dumps behind them are not — they are regenerable.
checkpoints/.facts-*.json

# ─── OS / tooling junk ───────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── (Belt-and-suspenders) any stray media at the root ───────────
# Leading slash = ROOT ONLY, which is what the heading always claimed. Without it
# these matched at every depth, so a reference image inside skills/ could not be
# tracked without `git add -f`. Anchored 2026-08-10 (ROADMAP known problem 6).
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.mp4
/*.mov
/*.wav
/*.ogg
/*.mp3
/*.webm
/*.m4a
